      "text": "To find the simplified form of \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\\), we start by expressing the radicand in terms of its prime factors:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{2^7} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{3^3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7}\\). We can write 27 as \\(2^7 = 2^4 \\cdot 2^3\\), so:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7} = \\sqrt[4]{2^4 \\cdot 2^3} = \\sqrt[4]{2^4} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2^3} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2^3} = 2 \\sqrt[4]{8}\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, we simplify \\(\\sqrt[4]{3^3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{3^2 \\cdot 3} = \\sqrt[4]{3^2} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{3} = \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{3}\n\\]\n\nCombining these results, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = 2 \\sqrt[4]{8} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{3} = 2 \\sqrt[4]{24}\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\\) simplifies to \\(2 \\sqrt[4]{24}\\). Here, \\(a = 2\\) and \\(b = 24\\). Therefore, the sum \\(a + b\\) is:\n\n\\[\na + b = 2 + 24 = 26\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26}\n\\]",
